# Commit / deploy policy — Cindy Oct 16, 2026

Canon: `loop/CCH_STUDIO_DEPLOY_RULE_CW_Oct16.md`. It replaces the Sep 25 rule where they conflict.

All sessions share ONE working copy at `C:\dev\CCH-Platform-Deploy\cch-deploy`. A commit here
sweeps up **every session's** uncommitted edits. A hosting deploy ships the whole `platform` folder.

## Staging — the builder chat does this
- The chat that builds a feature deploys it to **staging** and re-deploys staging after her fixes.
- Do not hand staging off to Cursor #1.
- Append the `_DEPLOY_QUEUE.md` line and mark it done with the staging time. Do not leave it pending for #1.

## Production — Cursor #1 only, after her typed GO
- Only Cursor #1 deploys to production, and only after Cindy's typed GO.
- Production bugs: #1 fixes and deploys straight to production after that GO. No staging lap.
- Before any production deploy, check what is already live so a newer live fix is not overwritten.
- Anything paid, ordered, or approved is locked. Never change it.

## Commits
- Do NOT run `git add`, `git commit`, `git push`, or `git stash` unless Cindy asks or you are #1 and she asked.
- `git pull` / `git fetch` / read-only `git status` are fine.

## Keep going
- Work the whole list. Stop only for her GO, a money question, or a real blocker.
- If it is not verified, say so. Do not make it up.
